0" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(P-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )(7-\\lambda )-1\\cdot (-5) & =0 \\\\ 49-7\\lambda -7\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+5 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-14\\lambda +54 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the discriminant of the quadratic equation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =(-14)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 54 \\\\  & =196-216 \\\\  & =-20 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the characteristic equation does not have real solutions and therefore $P$ does not have real eigenvalues." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-36780/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d235bca-d848-5075-affb-09e3103cfc11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-36780"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107852/selection/bdb0c7f5d4b7fe04d9e602641d68ea6fc24fa542d5f2becc060b84154e0c0aca" :answer/id #uuid "c5354561-6919-52db-b304-546938528e20" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107852/selection/5c6f15b46c223139f686cf0a40e221794c8e5b9780a96c4f4c2404b7dc8910f6" :answer/id #uuid "5c8bd375-ddcb-54f2-aaf0-bac3bedcf3a9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\lambda =43$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107852/selection/aae122e1f55c894290914bccee1ccec58d8c49d0901aa6f7687e625f18c27991" :answer/id #uuid "e003cfaa-e3b2-525f-9b4c-da1299d2fd76" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =13$ and $\\lambda =43$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107852/selection/5adf8aff07c26e1a4e2e77d8aa67ab3ab7c8d16bb10657ec6dfb99329a00a4ec" :answer/id #uuid "2e864fa6-2716-5653-b992-c76d1389180e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =13$ (double root)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107852/selection/595be931c35f13fe8fb066954139f3e5f7317d908cd2706f50acc3257fdd426c" :answer/id #uuid "d25d95a8-9dc9-5ea3-8c14-ca55a38c4923" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =43$ (double root)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107852/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "901f9a2b-e84a-5333-b611-b0d558fe65e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107852/selection/bdb0c7f5d4b7fe04d9e602641d68ea6fc24fa542d5f2becc060b84154e0c0aca" :answer-field/choices ["q-107852/selection/bdb0c7f5d4b7fe04d9e602641d68ea6fc24fa542d5f2becc060b84154e0c0aca" "q-107852/selection/5c6f15b46c223139f686cf0a40e221794c8e5b9780a96c4f4c2404b7dc8910f6" "q-107852/selection/aae122e1f55c894290914bccee1ccec58d8c49d0901aa6f7687e625f18c27991" "q-107852/selection/5adf8aff07c26e1a4e2e77d8aa67ab3ab7c8d16bb10657ec6dfb99329a00a4ec" "q-107852/selection/595be931c35f13fe8fb066954139f3e5f7317d908cd2706f50acc3257fdd426c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107852" :question/id #uuid "b2684b28-0c59-5171-ade6-34093aeb8db7" :question/math-academy-id "q-107852" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$Q=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 8\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $Q-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nQ-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -3 & 8-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(Q-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -3 & 8-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(8-\\lambda )-(-3)\\cdot 1 & =0 \\\\ 40-5\\lambda -8\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+3 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +43 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the discriminant of the quadratic equation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =(-13)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 43 \\\\  & =169-172 \\\\  & =-3 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the characteristic equation does not have real solutions and therefore $Q$ does not have real eigenvalues." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-107852/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d235bca-d848-5075-affb-09e3103cfc11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107852"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-36778/selection/7adbd65c950d59bfc3c55d87c0cd4e3bb35c291375e5db82650e1846115a141e" :answer/id #uuid "ca034c8a-7b28-56cf-ab40-578a22b15610" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\lambda =2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36778/selection/0cec3e602533c8a82e8cfc71f025c6aa7bf29c73f75f79493ec8c0ef98ec5e2c" :answer/id #uuid "66ee4662-bb53-5d74-8309-dbedd4a9ef42" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\lambda =-1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36778/selection/dd0193083dd9eaa34a32a51d77ca7d2a8dc11acd4fc6a936ddd851ea7a7705b1" :answer/id #uuid "b3bbd308-5322-5518-9e15-2babb35954b2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ (double root)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36778/selection/ba1d8375e1a83806a44d03a8ee41a12d5712c46f39031bbfa81bfd0881d57760" :answer/id #uuid "afe3c234-4e11-53c6-87d4-16c32c787dda" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$  (double root)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36778/selection/bdb0c7f5d4b7fe04d9e602641d68ea6fc24fa542d5f2becc060b84154e0c0aca" :answer/id #uuid "9d85bcbe-a76b-5262-81ff-7872bd626617" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36778/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7c1a0966-4032-53f1-a39e-b9b2aa22c11d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-36778/selection/ba1d8375e1a83806a44d03a8ee41a12d5712c46f39031bbfa81bfd0881d57760" :answer-field/choices ["q-36778/selection/7adbd65c950d59bfc3c55d87c0cd4e3bb35c291375e5db82650e1846115a141e" "q-36778/selection/0cec3e602533c8a82e8cfc71f025c6aa7bf29c73f75f79493ec8c0ef98ec5e2c" "q-36778/selection/dd0193083dd9eaa34a32a51d77ca7d2a8dc11acd4fc6a936ddd851ea7a7705b1" "q-36778/selection/ba1d8375e1a83806a44d03a8ee41a12d5712c46f39031bbfa81bfd0881d57760" "q-36778/selection/bdb0c7f5d4b7fe04d9e602641d68ea6fc24fa542d5f2becc060b84154e0c0aca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-36778" :question/id #uuid "3b14bc23-f539-5c26-97da-0a4a4fc1772d" :question/math-academy-id "q-36778" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$E=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ -2 & -6\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $E-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nE-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 8 \\\\ -2 & -6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(E-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(E-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 8 \\\\ -2 & -6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(-6-\\lambda )-(-2)\\cdot 8 & =0 \\\\ -12-2\\lambda +6\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $E$ has only one eigenvalue $\\lambda =-2,$ which is a double root of the characteristic equation." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-36778/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d235bca-d848-5075-affb-09e3103cfc11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-36778"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-36776"] :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$Q=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -10\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $Q-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nQ-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-6-\\lambda  & -3 \\\\ 2 & -10-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(Q-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-6-\\lambda  & -3 \\\\ 2 & -10-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-6-\\lambda )(-10-\\lambda )-(-3)\\cdot 2 & =0 \\\\ 60+6\\lambda +10\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+6 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+16\\lambda +66 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the discriminant of the quadratic equation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={16}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 66 \\\\  & =256-264 \\\\  & =-8 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the characteristic equation does not have real solutions, and therefore, $Q$ does not have real eigenvalues." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-76364/selection/4830da676a9354bf22610505475a50575325d02580050ba0171b20c20386082d" :answer/id #uuid "dd7e612d-504c-5b59-843d-09f92ad6a2b5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =-\\sqrt{7}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76364/selection/682f5c8b5d2a0f67317f18a7becd9159aee9bd16a0a765dbdfa1418902d99653" :answer/id #uuid "bc4938dd-735e-5f49-b85c-07c48a5d7804" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =6$ (double root)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76364/selection/bdb0c7f5d4b7fe04d9e602641d68ea6fc24fa542d5f2becc060b84154e0c0aca" :answer/id #uuid "1779872a-632b-5cb9-843b-554ea3bf75c1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76364/selection/9bae6c8b084be117d6ca22b2f4048ba506e2a1b95bfaee5996a3fa16c7c4ee2e" :answer/id #uuid "92c807b7-297c-5415-bd71-dc877203d1ea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =\\sqrt{7}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76364/selection/7709667945507ef0eaefdcc8cff82fb694e238da88a3266770528ce73bfded0c" :answer/id #uuid "d7af984b-e477-55e0-b830-64a4b5f50058" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =-\\sqrt{7}$ (double root)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76364/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "604dcb0f-2420-5377-8324-04c58a13063a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76364/selection/4830da676a9354bf22610505475a50575325d02580050ba0171b20c20386082d" :answer-field/choices ["q-76364/selection/4830da676a9354bf22610505475a50575325d02580050ba0171b20c20386082d" "q-76364/selection/682f5c8b5d2a0f67317f18a7becd9159aee9bd16a0a765dbdfa1418902d99653" "q-76364/selection/bdb0c7f5d4b7fe04d9e602641d68ea6fc24fa542d5f2becc060b84154e0c0aca" "q-76364/selection/9bae6c8b084be117d6ca22b2f4048ba506e2a1b95bfaee5996a3fa16c7c4ee2e" "q-76364/selection/7709667945507ef0eaefdcc8cff82fb694e238da88a3266770528ce73bfded0c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76364" :question/id #uuid "a400aa29-b613-5c26-88d6-532019155a9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-76364" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$N=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{7} & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $N-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nN-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{7}-\\lambda  & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(N-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(N-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{7}-\\lambda  & 6 \\\\ 0 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-\\sqrt{7}-\\lambda )(-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 6 & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda +\\sqrt{7}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =-\\sqrt{7}.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-76364/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd4158d-6baf-5a61-96a2-74c66231d082"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76364"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-11983"] :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -\\sqrt{3})(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\lambda =2.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-106995/selection/738cc9346b0e6505636b89804659d921ab8201d6573f95236bb961daec888223" :answer/id #uuid "e69c2b94-fd5a-5956-a0e8-60a8e558dfe7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =5$ (double root)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106995/selection/b15d54dacfcdb9421da6896e2e33a298663bebeaeb07f5289712fc137843418d" :answer/id #uuid "ede9ca59-93a1-58d5-86b4-008dff9bd072" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =5$ and $\\lambda =3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106995/selection/3a7eaa153cdf57e7843c8630a5cce3db6ad07134315ee4b8d414e4417837054b" :answer/id #uuid "147220da-5f19-590c-8df0-44c3d8c97c31" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =5$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106995/selection/15cc786dbcf35cc1016e35f342e50d0761e6bbdc88817e71cbb569fab12ae6b9" :answer/id #uuid "8e19d340-4e62-5539-a202-5a5a4a57f54d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ (double root)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106995/selection/bdb0c7f5d4b7fe04d9e602641d68ea6fc24fa542d5f2becc060b84154e0c0aca" :answer/id #uuid "fed3e408-fea6-5fee-923d-31d95f4d7b30" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106995/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d4b09a31-18bf-51a8-9be4-1317c9f48324" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106995/selection/b15d54dacfcdb9421da6896e2e33a298663bebeaeb07f5289712fc137843418d" :answer-field/choices ["q-106995/selection/738cc9346b0e6505636b89804659d921ab8201d6573f95236bb961daec888223" "q-106995/selection/b15d54dacfcdb9421da6896e2e33a298663bebeaeb07f5289712fc137843418d" "q-106995/selection/3a7eaa153cdf57e7843c8630a5cce3db6ad07134315ee4b8d414e4417837054b" "q-106995/selection/15cc786dbcf35cc1016e35f342e50d0761e6bbdc88817e71cbb569fab12ae6b9" "q-106995/selection/bdb0c7f5d4b7fe04d9e602641d68ea6fc24fa542d5f2becc060b84154e0c0aca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106995" :question/id #uuid "68216f82-a312-524f-becc-2374f6ca189d" :question/math-academy-id "q-106995" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 2 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -5)(\\lambda -3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =5$ and $\\lambda =3.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106995/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd4158d-6baf-5a61-96a2-74c66231d082"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106995"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106999/selection/3d320d30e440b15c335b6980c837f34365a5f1aeb26ad90ff9cfb67523d7ff30" :answer/id #uuid "3e502208-a850-5d05-bd93-d293a8fba1cf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =23$ (double root)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106999/selection/cc775a8705da88427b3de1e72c802bc135315e2f7f010856830f65c33d3f61bf" :answer/id #uuid "fdcdab46-6c64-5a2d-a2e6-8b7093dfb048" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =23$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106999/selection/debe05565d5f4a7374151e0e0855a973944529678055a1f093ae26c46aa26ffd" :answer/id #uuid "38844d2f-6851-5e63-a2eb-cf86b5db0b31" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\lambda =23$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106999/selection/bdb0c7f5d4b7fe04d9e602641d68ea6fc24fa542d5f2becc060b84154e0c0aca" :answer/id #uuid "55ed2e2f-d6c8-5e81-9916-fa53d876d6ad" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106999/selection/985ce9b79bfe260fc1b2f499987e7c601183126eb9352702fe93af28b231a320" :answer/id #uuid "2c71b747-e1a3-5f44-8110-e8b2787fe728" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =-8$ and $\\lambda =23$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106999/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "658127fa-7d23-57c7-a3c1-ca26136930a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106999/selection/cc775a8705da88427b3de1e72c802bc135315e2f7f010856830f65c33d3f61bf" :answer-field/choices ["q-106999/selection/3d320d30e440b15c335b6980c837f34365a5f1aeb26ad90ff9cfb67523d7ff30" "q-106999/selection/cc775a8705da88427b3de1e72c802bc135315e2f7f010856830f65c33d3f61bf" "q-106999/selection/debe05565d5f4a7374151e0e0855a973944529678055a1f093ae26c46aa26ffd" "q-106999/selection/bdb0c7f5d4b7fe04d9e602641d68ea6fc24fa542d5f2becc060b84154e0c0aca" "q-106999/selection/985ce9b79bfe260fc1b2f499987e7c601183126eb9352702fe93af28b231a320"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106999" :question/id #uuid "6bc4edb2-a90d-543d-9659-c11413861acf" :question/math-academy-id "q-106999" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$N=[\\begin{aligned}23 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $N-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nN-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}23-\\lambda  & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(N-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(N-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}23-\\lambda  & -8 \\\\ 0 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (23-\\lambda )(-\\lambda )-0\\cdot (-8) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -23) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =23.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106999/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd4158d-6baf-5a61-96a2-74c66231d082"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106999"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107843/selection/bf677808d99e769c7d0b42598a5869de6a1332f65b35e24418d0b0b7d650f058" :answer/id #uuid "65e90b5e-b386-5128-b61b-1376151666ec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =18$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107843/selection/730ff4b805bd534b362144172ec107a37343c09826336cc8f5ab1d3ecd8e21b5" :answer/id #uuid "1c537cc6-c052-57a9-b158-9535769d7f82" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =9$ (double root)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107843/selection/7f37ec7a7b79ec816432671262fe88541bfb000beee8ec0a624d9c08788e6f09" :answer/id #uuid "83fe7cc5-7e75-5083-b3f3-0b95a9410ffe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\lambda =18$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107843/selection/bdb0c7f5d4b7fe04d9e602641d68ea6fc24fa542d5f2becc060b84154e0c0aca" :answer/id #uuid "072c591e-a145-51dc-afa1-48e0f3783e40" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107843/selection/85cad96e6b4e6ce424f63a80423e09bd857654f7ecca7e86614ec61790cbcb72" :answer/id #uuid "b841752f-674d-5945-bb07-dd40bba48a18" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\lambda =9$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107843/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "85eed561-2f89-5991-807b-64207407a17e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107843/selection/bf677808d99e769c7d0b42598a5869de6a1332f65b35e24418d0b0b7d650f058" :answer-field/choices ["q-107843/selection/bf677808d99e769c7d0b42598a5869de6a1332f65b35e24418d0b0b7d650f058" "q-107843/selection/730ff4b805bd534b362144172ec107a37343c09826336cc8f5ab1d3ecd8e21b5" "q-107843/selection/7f37ec7a7b79ec816432671262fe88541bfb000beee8ec0a624d9c08788e6f09" "q-107843/selection/bdb0c7f5d4b7fe04d9e602641d68ea6fc24fa542d5f2becc060b84154e0c0aca" "q-107843/selection/85cad96e6b4e6ce424f63a80423e09bd857654f7ecca7e86614ec61790cbcb72"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107843" :question/id #uuid "516deea5-c1fd-59bf-8d83-57450943e342" :question/math-academy-id "q-107843" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$N=[\\begin{aligned}18 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $N-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nN-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}18-\\lambda  & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(N-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(N-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}18-\\lambda  & -5 \\\\ 0 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (18-\\lambda )(-\\lambda )-0\\cdot (-5) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -18) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =18.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-107843/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd4158d-6baf-5a61-96a2-74c66231d082"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107843"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5479"] :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/901d3a22065b48a8076b9c9aae5563c770c36c9ad40e4063c0f739847e1cda98.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\, A-\\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/0c6f9f860a1cf4d510f6c3d4d9c66b77496a354bb1e2cef1b69fd1178e4f15ab.png)\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-4\\cdot 3 & =0 \\\\ 4-4\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-12 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda -8 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5481"] :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/a1b88b7897649bb059cef39d40b2b052a13ac28282223b5688a1bce98296fb53.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $A - \\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/ca8f02e390e338b62956302ec45ea274ad73a51dafde3fe93b3d1e37dd663699.png)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det(A-\\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}10-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 6 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (10-\\lambda )(7-\\lambda )-3\\cdot 6 & =0 \\\\ 70-7\\lambda -10\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-18 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-17\\lambda +52 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{17\\pm \\sqrt{(-17)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 52}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pm \\sqrt{81}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pm 9}{2} \\\\  & =13,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda=13$ and $\\lambda=4.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5480"] :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/5ca3e07cfbe9e5d4956b1eab4393601f2a78b0b067d17312e71cbac993e28a86.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $B-\\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/fdbcc62870aefab6214b2f24f53e9bc5654e5386639d4bc328dff3769aff2b45.png)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det(B-\\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $B$ has only one eigenvalue $\\lambda=4,$ which is a double root of the characteristic equation. \n\n**Note:** We also say that $\\lambda=4$ has an **algebraic multiplicity** of $2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5482"] :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/603c59d43e3be000931e7279ac4d27be8aa92692f1528ec57ebd52172affa3cb.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $A - \\lambda I \\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/f91e4886c58db10f60fa666a870aed3c2f456b25e6afb560f857e9c36e81217c.png)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det (A - \\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 9 & -2\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(-2\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda )-9\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2\\sqrt{3}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the eigenvalues $\\lambda={\\color{red}3}$ and $\\lambda={\\color{blue}-2\\sqrt{3}}.$\n\nIf we look again at the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068962/assets/aa89b93c6fabd2f3dc7063c85e253ded7482018a5f1c6dadedc74964194c5754.png)\nwe see that the eigenvalues are the entries on the main diagonal. This is true in general: the eigenvalues of a *triangular* or *diagonal* matrix are *always* given by the entries on the main diagonal!\n\n**Watch out!** For a general matrix (which is neither triangular nor diagonal), this might not be the case!" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
